===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|fœderalism}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|fédéralisme}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|federal|ism}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A {{l|en|system}} of {{l|en|national}} {{l|en|government}} in which {{l|en|power}} is {{l|en|divided}} between a {{l|en|central}} {{l|en|authority}} and a number of {{l|en|regions}} with [[delimited]] [[self-governing]] authority.
# The [[belief]] that [[such]] a [[system]] is [[superior]] to [[other]] [[form]]s of [[government]].
# {{lb|en|theology}} [[covenantalism|Covenantalism]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|belief in the superiority of wide regional autonomy}} {{l|en|regionalism}}, {{l|en|provincialism}}, {{l|en|statism}}

